Conclusion and Next Steps

This document provided a detailed inspection and change plan for migrating FitSite to the unified “all-in-one” development branch structure. We covered database alignment (ensuring code matches the schema , etc.), backend logic updates (with new endpoints and calculations), and frontend GUI changes (with references to the new design).

 

By following these guidelines, a developer should be able to systematically update the codebase:

Update Models/Database code – adjust table names, fields, and relations in code to match the schema.

Adjust Business Logic – implement calculations for 1RM and volume, enforce new constraints, add new features like goals and metrics handling.

Revise API Routes – unify endpoint patterns (under /api perhaps) and ensure the frontend uses them.

Revamp Frontend Components – implement the new login, dashboard, and profile UI, integrating all new data flows.

Test End-to-End – verify that a user can do everything in the new system and that data consistency is maintained.

